  "description": "QUMKES crystallizes in the tetragonal crystal system with space group I 41/a. Reported CIF formula moiety: C320 H360 N16 Nd4 O64 Zn8 4+,2(C6 H12 N4 Nd2 O20 2-),x(C4 H10 O1),y(C2 H6 O1),z(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Zn1 (Zn) has 3 O neighbors; Zn2 (Zn) has 3 O neighbors; Nd1 (Nd) has 10 O neighbors; Zn3 (Zn) has 3 O neighbors; Zn4 (Zn) has 3 O neighbors; Nd3 (Nd) has 10 O neighbors; Zn5 (Zn) has 3 O neighbors; Zn6 (Zn) has 3 O neighbors; Nd4 (Nd) has 10 O neighbors; Zn7 (Zn) has 3 O neighbors; Zn8 (Zn) has 3 O neighbors; Nd5 (Nd) has 10 O neighbors; Nd2 (Nd) has 9 O neighbors; Nd6 (Nd) has 9 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 9 pairs, 5 components; largest component is a chain with approximately linear metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.598-4.157 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 103.44-111.69°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Zn8Nd4L8(OAc)8][Nd2(OAc)3(NO3)4(OH)(H2O)]2 (L = 8,8'-((1E,1'E)-(((octane-1,8-diylbis(oxy))bis(2,1-phenylene))bis(azaneylylidene))bis(methaneylylidene))bis(2-ethoxyphenolate); solvated diethyl ether/ethanol/water). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 8 OAc (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 3 OAc (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 1 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 1 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula). Article name explicitly identifies I(I), I(II).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
